import Polyplets.DepthOneKernelUnique
import Polyplets.DepthOneSeries

-- Machine-generated polynomial literals are longer than the style line
-- limit by nature; see the module docstring for their provenance.
set_option linter.style.longLine false

/-!
# Notary piece K, module 9: the kernel closed form annihilates `Φ`

Campaign *Notary*, piece **K** of `docs/notary-k-plan.md`, wave K-δ, the
capstone.  The six walk unknowns are the transcribed closed forms
(`DepthOneKernelSol` / `DepthOneKernelUnique`); assembled through
`F₁ = P̂ − B²/(3+S)` they give the rational `s`-series `phiF1` with unit
denominator `phiDen` (constant term `-42336`).  This module carries `phiF1`
to the exact defect statement `Φ(x, N(x)) = 0`, upgrading
`DepthOneSeries.phi_annihilates` (a `native_decide` check mod `x⁶¹`) to an
exact power-series identity.

## The quartic is one scalar certificate

The whole `y`-form quartic collapses to a single scalar elimination identity
in `ℚ⟦s⟧` modulo `A² = 1−2X−3X²` and `B² = 1+2X−3X²`.  With
`numTuple = n0 + n1 A + n2 B + n3 A B` and `dd = numTuple − n0`,

    (dd² + Pq)² = 4·(1−2X−3X²)·(dd·n1 + n2 n3 (1+2X−3X²))²,

`Pq = n1² AA − n2² BB − n3² AA BB`.  This is `Ψ(numTuple) = 0`; a single
`linear_combination` over `Kernel.A_sq` / `Kernel.B_sq` closes it (cofactors
17872 / 8122 chars, the same regime as `Sol` / `Unique`).  Generated and
re-verified as a free-polynomial identity by
`experiments/notary_kdelta_gen6.py` (`build/notary_kdelta_phi_cert.txt`).

## The lift (design note)

`PowerSeries.rescale` does **not** exist in this Mathlib.  The `x ↦ 3x`
scaling is done coefficient-wise, exactly as `DepthOneSeries.nSeries`
already does: `N` has coefficient `k = 3^(k+1)·[yᵏ]F₁ + [k=0]`.  `phiF1`
is even in `s` (`n0, den, n3` even; `n1, n2` are mirror images through
`A ↔ B` under `s ↦ −s`), so it descends to the `y`-series
`F1y k = coeff (2k) phiF1`.  `Φ(x, N) = 3·Σ_k cY_k(3x)·((N−1)/3)^k` by the
`ring` identity `3·Σ cY_k(3x)((W−1)/3)^k = Σ phiC_k(x) Wᵏ` (verified in
gen6); the `×3` coefficient hom `mk (fun n => 3ⁿ · coeff n ·)` is
multiplicative (`3ⁿ = 3ⁱ·3ʲ`), which is all the lift needs.
-/

namespace Polyplets
namespace DepthOneKernelPhi

open PowerSeries

/-! ## Generated closed-form literals (`experiments/notary_kdelta_gen6.py`) -/

noncomputable def phiN0 : PowerSeries ℚ := 17892 + (-153009) * X ^ 2 + (-93771) * X ^ 4 + 199066 * X ^ 6 + (-38478) * X ^ 8 + (-32761) * X ^ 10 + 10197 * X ^ 12 + (-1296) * X ^ 14
noncomputable def phiN1 : PowerSeries ℚ := (-1764) + (-6948) * X + (-5931) * X ^ 2 + (-3699) * X ^ 3 + 36 * X ^ 4 + 8748 * X ^ 5 + 4234 * X ^ 6 + (-362) * X ^ 7 + (-3532) * X ^ 8 + (-2096) * X ^ 9 + 921 * X ^ 10 + 261 * X ^ 11 + (-108) * X ^ 12
noncomputable def phiN2 : PowerSeries ℚ := (-1764) + 6948 * X + (-5931) * X ^ 2 + 3699 * X ^ 3 + 36 * X ^ 4 + (-8748) * X ^ 5 + 4234 * X ^ 6 + 362 * X ^ 7 + (-3532) * X ^ 8 + 2096 * X ^ 9 + 921 * X ^ 10 + (-261) * X ^ 11 + (-108) * X ^ 12
noncomputable def phiN3 : PowerSeries ℚ := (-252) + 2223 * X ^ 2 + 684 * X ^ 4 + (-2618) * X ^ 6 + 992 * X ^ 8 + (-261) * X ^ 10
noncomputable def phiDen : PowerSeries ℚ := (-42336) + 364860 * X ^ 2 + 197424 * X ^ 4 + (-481476) * X ^ 6 + 118160 * X ^ 8 + 68580 * X ^ 10 + (-23328) * X ^ 12 + 2916 * X ^ 14
noncomputable def phiPq : PowerSeries ℚ := ((-63504) + 36578304 * X + 1755432 * X ^ 2 + (-232937856) * X ^ 3 + (-16372449) * X ^ 4 + (-893579040) * X ^ 5 + 51692922 * X ^ 6 + 94703472 * X ^ 7 + 13904163 * X ^ 8 + 1419509520 * X ^ 9 + (-156922776) * X ^ 10 + (-546940800) * X ^ 11 + 107600606 * X ^ 12 + (-865492224) * X ^ 13 + 67411932 * X ^ 14 + 712137568 * X ^ 15 + (-121317426) * X ^ 16 + (-86920096) * X ^ 17 + 73984864 * X ^ 18 + (-85147264) * X ^ 19 + (-26402301) * X ^ 20 + 33556896 * X ^ 21 + 5341626 * X ^ 22 + (-5190480) * X ^ 23 + (-613089) * X ^ 24 + 291600 * X ^ 25)

/-- `numTuple − n0 = n1 A + n2 B + n3 A B`. -/
noncomputable def dd : PowerSeries ℚ :=
  phiN1 * Kernel.A + phiN2 * Kernel.B + phiN3 * Kernel.A * Kernel.B

/-- The kernel closed form `n0 + n1 A + n2 B + n3 A B`. -/
noncomputable def numTuple : PowerSeries ℚ := phiN0 + dd

/-- The assembled depth-1 defect series `F₁` in the `s`-variable. -/
noncomputable def phiF1 : PowerSeries ℚ := numTuple * (phiDen)⁻¹

/-! ## The scalar quartic (the certificate)

`(dd² + Pq)² = 4 AA (dd n1 + n2 n3 BB)²`, one `linear_combination` over the
two square relations.  This is the whole elimination; everything downstream
consumes it. -/

